# DRAFT / UNVERIFIED (Oracle Migration Sprint, Phase 6) -- no real domain
# or DNS record exists yet for the Oracle VM as of this draft. Replace
# api.example-vidhidesk.com below with the real domain once one is
# registered and its A/AAAA record points at the Oracle VM's public IP,
# then run `caddy validate --config /path/to/this/file` and reload Caddy
# on the box itself. This file has never been applied to or tested
# against a live Caddy instance.
#
# Caddy handles ACME/Let's Encrypt HTTPS automatically for any real
# domain listed as a site block below -- no separate certbot setup
# needed, and plain-HTTP requests on port 80 are redirected to HTTPS
# automatically for any domain block (not the bare-IP :80 block below).
#
# Port 8000 (the FastAPI container from api/Dockerfile) is intentionally
# never exposed directly to the internet -- only Caddy's 443/80 are, per
# the Oracle Migration Sprint's safety rules. Bind Docker's -p flag to
# 127.0.0.1:8000 (see deploy/oracle_deploy.sh), not 0.0.0.0:8000, so this
# reverse proxy is the only path in even before firewall rules are
# double-checked.

api.example-vidhidesk.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000

	encode gzip

	log {
		output file /var/log/caddy/vidhidesk-api-access.log
	}
}

# Fallback while no domain/DNS exists yet: serves plain HTTP on the box's
# bare IP so the deploy pipeline's own health/drift checks have something
# to hit before Phase 6 (domain + HTTPS) is actually done. Remove this
# block once the domain above is live -- it deliberately does NOT get
# HTTPS (Caddy only issues certificates for named domains, never for a
# bare IP), so it must not be the long-term production path.
:80 {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
